# Improved SMPL (0.2.0-experimental, then named Fine Tune + Sample Rate): a plain turn of TUN (knob A, SAMPLE page) moves
# 1 cent a step, as many steps as stock's semitones: the same nudges moved 0.1.1 (emulator,
# 10 Nov 2026) +4 then -6 semitones (`nudge +3` takes 4 steps here, acceleration); here they move
# +4 cents (word 0x400a, reads +0.04) then -6 (0x3ffa, -0.02); the TUN word is BD's target,
# 0x8000e5d2. Back on a whole semitone it reads (0), as LFO depth does at zero. CC 24 64 then clears
# cents from +0.04 (word 0x4000).
# Changes BD's TUN by CC 24 and puts it back to +0 (CC 24 64).
# SMPL is pressed from AMP, never on its own page (that toggles the knob and waveform views), so
# the SAMPLE page keeps the view it had: the unit references are its waveform view.
name: sample-rate-fine-tun
state: changes

hold TRK
key BD
release TRK
key AMP
wait 300
key SMPL
wait 3500
cc 24 64
wait 300
nudge A +3
wait 750
screen plus4
expect plus4 == ref region 0 9 34 9
mem t4 0x8000e5d2 2
expect t4 == 400a
nudge A -5
wait 750
screen minus2
expect minus2 == ref region 0 9 34 9
mem tm2 0x8000e5d2 2
expect tm2 == 3ffa
nudge A +2
wait 750
screen whole
expect whole == ref region 0 9 34 9
mem t0 0x8000e5d2 2
expect t0 == 4000
nudge A +3
wait 750
cc 24 64
wait 300
mem tcc 0x8000e5d2 2
expect tcc == 4000
